---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Claude Opus 5 — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="Anthropic's default start for most workloads."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Frontier models</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Claude Opus 5</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Claude Opus 5 is Anthropic’s default start for most workloads: complex agentic coding and enterprise work. The API id is <code>claude-opus-5</code>. Pricing is $5 input and $25 output per million tokens.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Anthropic lists a reliable knowledge and training data cutoff of May 2026. Parameter count, training FLOPs, and the full post-training recipe for this SKU are not published on the models overview or choosing guide.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Adaptive thinking is supported. Default effort is <code>high</code>. Relative to the current Claude lineup, Opus sits in a moderate latency class. Effort steers how much the model thinks.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1 million tokens. Max output is 128K tokens. Inputs are text and images; output is text. The model supports multilingual use, vision, and tool use.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Anthropic’s choosing guide names an effort parameter, tools, and computer-use class workloads for Opus 5.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Numbers below are from Anthropic’s Fable 5.1 announce (Opus 5 column). OpenAI’s Sol and Astra tables use different harnesses, so treat those as separate prints.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Eval</th><th scope="col">Opus 5</th><th scope="col">Fable 5.1</th><th scope="col">Fable 5</th><th scope="col">GPT-5.6 Sol (Anthropic column)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1</td><td>29.0%</td><td>52.6%</td><td>24.7%</td><td>22.4%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench 4.0</td><td>52.3%</td><td>55.8%</td><td>42.0%</td><td>37.3%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GDPval-AA v2 (score)</td><td>1824</td><td>1853</td><td>1723</td><td>1711</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OSWorld 2.0 partial</td><td>75.4%</td><td>77.9%</td><td>72.9%</td><td>-</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OSWorld 2.0 strict</td><td>39.6%</td><td>41.7%</td><td>36.1%</td><td>-</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Humanity&#x27;s Last Exam (no tools)</td><td>56.6%</td><td>60.9%</td><td>57.8%</td><td>-</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Humanity&#x27;s Last Exam (with tools)</td><td>63.6%</td><td>65.0%</td><td>63.8%</td><td>-</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AutomationBench</td><td>26.9%</td><td>31.4%</td><td>17.1%</td><td>19.6%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>CursorBench 3.2.0</td><td>70.0%</td><td>73.4%</td><td>70.5%</td><td>67.2%</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Anthropic notes a Terminal-Bench-Science standard error of about ±3.5–4.5 points. OSWorld 2.0 is the August 2026 task release, not comparable to older OSWorld 2.0 prints. Anthropic notes biology tasks that hit Fable safeguards were completed by Opus 5.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>Anthropic trains and runs Claude on AWS Trainium, Google TPUs, and NVIDIA GPUs. Amazon is the primary cloud and training partner. Anthropic reported more than 1 million Trainium2 chips in use as of April 2026. Per-SKU serving silicon is not published. Buyers purchase API tokens, not a named Claude GPU SKU.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Pricing is $5 input and $25 output per million tokens on the Claude API and partner clouds.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/overview">Models overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/choosing-a-model">Choosing a model</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-1">Introducing Claude Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1</a> (includes Opus 5 capability columns)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-amazon-compute">Amazon compute partnership (20 Apr 2026)</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/google-broadcom-partnership-compute">Google/Broadcom compute partnership (6 Apr 2026)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
